</Field Guns Equipment>

<overview>
<p>Mechanized wheeled platoons transport their infantry in wheeled armored personnel carriers optimized for speed on roads and improved surfaces. Wheeled APCs are cheaper to maintain and faster on pavement than tracked alternatives, making these platoons ideal for garrison rapid-response forces, highway patrol, and urban security operations. Their off-road capability is limited compared to tracked vehicles, restricting employment in rough terrain, but on developed worlds with good road networks, wheeled mechanized infantry offer the best balance of speed, protection, and operating cost.</p><p>Taking full advantage of the carrying capacity of the fighting vehicles, these platoons carry support machine guns to provide heavy firepower against a variety of targets in both offensive and defensive roles. Some are equipped with up-armored vehicles and heavier body armor, allowing these teams to assault well protected objectives and hold critical positions as long as possible.<p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on introduction date of ballistic plate armor.
</notes>

